# Implementation Plan: Fix Migration Corruption

## Goal Description
Restore missing columns in the `projects` table definition within the initial migration file [1325bf383954_initial_migration.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/alembic/versions/1325bf383954_initial_migration.py). These columns were inadvertently removed during a previous update, causing Alembic to fail during startup and resulting in a 502 Bad Gateway error.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Migrations

#### [MODIFY] [1325bf383954_initial_migration.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/SynapsePlan/backend/alembic/versions/1325bf383954_initial_migration.py)
Restore the following columns to the `projects` table:
- `id`
- `name`
- `description`
- `start_date`
- `end_date`
- `progress`
- `status`
- `created_at`
- `updated_at`

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- Run `docker-compose down -v` to clear the corrupted database.
- Run `docker-compose up --build -d` to rebuild and restart the environment.
- Check `docker logs synapseplan-backend-1` to ensure migrations complete successfully.
- Verify that the login page is reachable and backend docs are available at `http://localhost:8000/docs`.

### Manual Verification
- Log in as admin@synapseplan.com / admin.
- Create a project and a task.
- Update the task and verify changes persist.
- Verify the "Admin" link is visible in the sidebar.
